==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The [[Image:CfdOF_MeshRegion.svg|24px]] '''CfdOF MeshRegion''' command creates an object that holds data to add surface, volume and extrusion refinements to a background mesh. The data can be edited in a task panel.

==Usage== <!--T:5-->

===Create refinement data object=== <!--T:6-->

<!--T:7-->
# Select a [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] [[CfdOF_MeshFromShape|'''[GeometryName]_Mesh''' data object]] in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]].
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:CfdOF_MeshRegion.svg|16px]] [[CfdOF_MeshRegion|Mesh‏‎ refinement]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|CfdOF → [[Image:CfdOF_MeshRegion.svg|16px]] Mesh‏‎ refinement}} option from the menu.
# A [[Image:CfdOF_MeshRegion.svg|16px]] '''MeshRefinement''' data object is added to the [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] '''[GeometryName]_Mesh''' data object.
# The task panel opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information.
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to confirm and finish the command.
# Optionally repeat the command to add more refinement data objects to the [[Image:CfdOF_MeshFromShape.svg|16px]] '''[GeometryName]_Mesh''' data object.

===Edit refinement data object=== <!--T:8-->

<!--T:9-->
# Double-click a [[Image:CfdOF_MeshRegion.svg|16px]] '''MeshRefinement''' data object in Tree View.
# The task panel opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information.
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button to confirm and finish the command.

